 {
  "kind": "quote",
  "text": "今天把书架上的旧杂志剪了一下午。最有意思的不是剪下来的图，而是剪完之后桌上那些边角料：半个标题、一角天空、一截被裁掉的手指。它们单独看什么都不是，凑在一起却像一首没写完的诗。收藏夹大概也是这样，真正有价值的常常不是某一条，而是某几条恰好放在一起时，突然多出来的那一点意思。下次整理的时候，先别急着删，先把它们摊开。",
  "source": "随手记",
  "createdAt": 1785413877,
  "x": 1920,
  "y": 1604,
  "width": 220,
  "rotation": -3.0,
  "height": 286,
  "en": {
   "text": "I spent the afternoon cutting up old magazines from the bookshelf. The most interesting part wasn’t the pictures I cut out but the scraps left on the table: half a headline, a corner of sky, a cropped-off finger. On their own they’re nothing; together they read like an unfinished poem. A collection is probably the same. What matters most is often not any single item but the bit of extra meaning that appears when a few happen to sit side by side. Next time I tidy up, I won’t rush to delete. I’ll spread them out first.",
   "source": "A note to self"
  }
 },
